# profile: llama-cpp
# @tier: 1
# @summary: llama.cpp `llama-server`, one instance for chat and one for embeddings.
# @key: none. Chat:   llama-server -m <chat.gguf> --jinja --port 8089 -c 32768
#   Embed:  llama-server -m <nomic-embed-text-v1.5.gguf> --embeddings --port 8088
#   (--jinja is what enables tool calling; the ports avoid the agents' 8081 to 8085)
# @cost: free (your hardware)
# @dotnet: yes
# @verified: NOT VERIFIED. Documented from llama.cpp's OpenAI-compatible server only; this repo has not run it.
# @evals: live quality and safety suites through the eval CLI, capability check. Cost is null (unpriced).
# @judge: a local model should not grade itself. Suggestion only, not calibrated (D-7, M3).
# @judge-env: JUDGE_PROVIDER=openai JUDGE_MODEL=gpt-5.1
# 768-wide embeddings: see the ollama profile for the one-time dimension reset.
LLM_PROVIDER=openai
LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8089/v1
LLM_API=chat_completions
LLM_MODEL=local-model
OPENAI_API_KEY=not-needed
EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=openai_compatible
EMBEDDING_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8088/v1
EMBEDDING_API_KEY=not-needed
EMBEDDING_MODEL=nomic-embed-text-v1.5
EMBEDDING_DIM=768
